# FocusForest — Cursor Rules

## Project
FocusForest backend. Node.js + Express + TypeScript + Prisma + Supabase + Redis.
Building backend only. No frontend yet.

## Core mechanic (never get this wrong)
One tree per day. Stage progress = (focus_minutes / 25) × task_multiplier.
task_multiplier: completed=1.5, carried=1.0, none=1.0.
This formula runs SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Never suggest putting it on the client.

## Non-negotiable rules
- Score engine is server-side only
- JWT tokens go in httpOnly cookies, never localStorage
- Every POST body validated with Zod before touching Prisma
- All session submissions include client_session_id (UUID) for deduplication
- Midnight cron batches by user utc_offset — never a single UTC cron
- Use Prisma for all DB queries

## Stack
- Node.js 20, Express 4, TypeScript 5
- Prisma 5 → Supabase PostgreSQL
- Supabase Auth (JWT)
- Supabase Realtime (group live sessions)
- Redis via Upstash (leaderboard sorted sets + BullMQ)
- node-cron (midnight reset job)
- BullMQ (push notification queue)
- Railway (hosting)

## Key tables
users, sessions, daily_trees, streaks, groups, group_members, push_subscriptions

## API base
/api/v1 — all routes require Bearer JWT except /auth/signup and /auth/login

## When generating code
- Always check if a Prisma schema exists before writing queries
- Always add Zod schema before the route handler
- Prefer async/await over .then()
- Use try/catch with typed errors
- Never suggest client-side score calculation
- Never use any — use proper TypeScript types
